<setup>

  <selectFromSequence name="P" from="2500" to="5000" step="500"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="r" from="0.04" to="0.08" step="0.01"/>

  <function name="A">$P*e^($r*x)</function>
  <derivative name="AP">$A</derivative>

</setup>

  <p>Let <m>A(t)</m> represent the amount of money in an investment account, in dollars, at time <m>t</m> in years, where <m>t = 0</m> corresponds to <m>2015</m>.  Assume that a single investment was made at <m>t = 0</m> and that the increases are due to interest earnings.  The following table shows some of the values of <m>A(t)</m>.</p>
   <!--  <p>Note that <m>a = $a</m> and <m>b = $b</m>. </p> -->

      <tabular bottom="minor" top="minor">
        <row bottom="minor">
          <cell><m>t</m></cell>
          <cell><m>0</m></cell>
          <cell><m>2</m></cell>
          <cell><m>4</m></cell>
          <cell><m>6</m></cell>
          <cell><m>8</m></cell>
          <cell><m>10</m></cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell><m>A(t)</m></cell>
          <cell><math name="A0" displayDecimals="2">$$A(0)</math></cell>
          <cell><math name="A2" displayDecimals="2">$$A(2)</math></cell>
          <cell><math name="A4" displayDecimals="2">$$A(4)</math></cell>
          <cell><math name="A6" displayDecimals="2">$$A(6)</math></cell>
          <cell><math name="A8" displayDecimals="2">$$A(8)</math></cell>
          <cell><math name="A10" displayDecimals="2">$$A(10)</math></cell>
        </row>
      </tabular>

<p>
  <ol marker="a.">
    <li>
      <setup>
        <math simplify name="cd1">($A6-$A2)/(4) </math>
        <math simplify name="cd2">($A10-$A6)/(4) </math>
      </setup>
      <p>
        Use a central difference to find the best estimate you can for <m>A'(4)</m>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer><mathInput name="ans1"><label><m>A'(4) \approx</m></label></mathInput>
          <award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute>
            <when>
              $ans1 = $cd1
            </when>
          </award>
        </answer></p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        Similarly, use a central difference to find the best estimate you can for <m>A'(8)</m>.
      </p>
      <p><answer><mathInput name="ans2"><label><m>A'(8) \approx</m></label></mathInput>
          <award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute>
            <when>
              $ans2 = $cd2
            </when>
          </award>
        </answer></p>
    </li>
    <li sectionWideCheckWork forceIndividualAnswerColoring>
      <p>
        Complete the following sentences to explain the meaning of select data in the table and the derivative values you found in (a) and (b).
      </p>
      <p>
        At the start of the year <answer><shortDescription>year corresponding to t equals 4</shortDescription><award>2019</award></answer>, the value of the money in the account is <answer><shortDescription>value in account at the start of that year</shortDescription><award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute>$A4</award></answer> dollars, and its value is changing at an instantaneous rate of <answer><shortDescription>rate of change of value in the account in that year</shortDescription><award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.1" allowedErrorIsAbsolute>$cd1</award></answer> dollars per year. At the start of the year <answer><shortDescription>year corresponding to t equals 8</shortDescription><award>2023</award></answer>, the value of the money in the account is <answer><shortDescription>value in account at the start of that year</shortDescription><award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute>$A8</award></answer> dollars, and its value is changing at an instantaneous rate of <answer><shortDescription>rate of change of money in the account in that year</shortDescription><award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.1" allowedErrorIsAbsolute>$cd2</award></answer> dollars per year.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</p>